<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan foreign exchange trade to resume on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Taiwan foreign exchange trade to resume on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's foreign exchange market was closed on Monday for the final day of the five-day Chinese lunar new year holiday. Trading resumes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On the last day of trading last Wednesday, the Taiwan dollar ended at T$27.508 against Tuesday's T$27.438 finish.</p>
<p>Turnover through dealers was a heavy US$317.5 million.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
